  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday) \nIssued at 1042 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nHigh temperatures are expected to remain in the upper 90s and low \n100s Friday through the weekend, but storm chances will generally \ntrend downward as the upper level ridge repositions farther west and \npushes the best moisture back into NM. Still, a few isolated \ndiurnally driven storms may still occur Friday and Saturday \nafternoon/evening especially near the TX/NM state line. \nConfidence is fairly high that warmer than normal temperatures \nwill continue into at least early next week with storm chances \nremaining minimal. Model spread then increases slightly thereafter\nwith differences in the evolution of the upper ridge. A majority \nof solutions currently favor a continuation of hot and dry \nweather, with a subset of ensemble members indicating a return of \nslightly better moisture and low precipitation chances by the \nmiddle of next week. The drier outcome is currently favored with \nunseasonably warm temperatures still looking likely to continue.",
